> ## **In-Depth Analysis**
> 
> *RNA Codon Expansion and Protein Engineering*
> 
> The recent developments in RNA editing to expand codon usage have opened new avenues for protein engineering. This method leverages pseudouridine codon insertion into mRNA transcripts, paired with engineered decoder tRNA, to incorporate novel amino acids into proteins. This represents a significant advancement that could revolutionize the fields of synthetic biology and medicine. By surpassing existing limitations in protein engineering, these innovations hold potential for creating proteins with novel functionalities, which could impact drug design and therapeutic interventions [52955].
